## Node.js built-ins

Cortex has **no runtime npm dependencies**. It uses only Node.js built-in modules
(`fs`, `http`, `crypto`, `zlib`, `node:sqlite`, `node:test`, …), which are covered
by the Node.js license (MIT plus third-party components listed in that distribution).

`electron` appears in `devDependencies` only, for the optional desktop wrapper
(`npm run desktop:native`). It is not bundled or required at runtime.
